# Board selection (the project's dual-board switch).
#
# The Kconfig value selects the board's APP-SIDE behaviour (the P4-only
# code paths gate on CONFIG_BOARD_P4); the build target (IDF_TARGET)
# selects the partition table and the BSP component. The two must agree —
# the root CMakeLists FATAL_ERRORs on a mismatch.
#
# A project-ROOT Kconfig.projbuild is NOT processed by the ESP-IDF 5.5
# build system (only per-component Kconfig / Kconfig.projbuild files are
# collected, tools/cmake/kconfig.cmake), so the choice lives here, in the
# always-built board-shim component.
choice BOARD
    prompt "Board"
    default BOARD_S3

config BOARD_S3
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75 (466x466)"
    help
        The original board: 466x466 CO5300 QSPI AMOLED, CST9217 touch,
        PCF85063A RTC + TCA9554 expander, QMI8658C IMU, built-in Wi-Fi.
        16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM (not SPI-DMA-capable).

config BOARD_P4
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-XC (720x720)"
    help
        The 4C board: 720x720 JD9365 MIPI-DSI, GT911 touch, remote C6
        Wi-Fi over SDIO (esp_hosted / esp_wifi_remote), ES8311 codec,
        NO RTC IC / IO expander / IMU. The time base is the 32 kHz
        crystal RTC timer + SNTP; alarms are software esp_timer.
        32 MB flash, 32 MB PSRAM.
endchoice

# --- Component-manager if-clause guard keys (esp_hosted registry manifests) ---
#
# The esp_hosted 3.x manifests on the registry declare optional USB-host
# transport dependencies (espressif/usb_host_cdc_acm,
# cherry-embedded/cherryusb, espressif/iot_usbh_rndis), each gated by
# `if: ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_*_MANIFEST` — Kconfig symbols defined only in
# esp_hosted 3.x's own Kconfig. The version solver evaluates the if-clauses
# of EVERY candidate version while resolving (esp_wifi_remote 0.14.5
# depends on esp_hosted >=0.0.6, an unbounded range), so those clauses are
# parsed against this project's sdkconfig.json even though the tree pins
# esp_hosted 1.4.7 (which does not define the symbols). Since esp_hosted
# 3.1.0 (2026-11-05) landed on the registry, a re-resolution therefore hit
# the interface-v4 "missing required kconfig option" fatal (prepare.py
# exit 10). Defining the three keys here makes the clauses evaluate to
# false (the C6 is transported over SDIO — no USB host backend) instead of
# aborting the configure. They must be INT, not bool: the clauses compare
# against 1 ($CONFIG{...} == 1), and the if-clause parser (if_parser.py)
# dispatches on the sdkconfig.json value type — a bool value makes it
# eval_bool("1"), a hard "Invalid boolean" error; an int value is a
# normal 0 == 1 comparison.
config ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_CDC_ACM_MANIFEST
    int
    default 0

config ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_CHERRYUSB_MANIFEST
    int
    default 0

config ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_RNDIS_MANIFEST
    int
    default 0
